atlas optimization-estate-physical-density

architecture estate-physical-density
  canonical_name EstatePhysicalDensity
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Estate density
  layer storage
  semantic_question How much physical disk can the five storage estates (models, releases, estate-local, operator, caches) give back without changing a path or a byte that a receipt, release or reader names?
  purpose Converge cold estate files onto filesystem-level dense representations, APFS clones for byte-identical files and APFS transparent (decmpfs) compression for compressible cold files, so every reader sees the same path and the same bytes while allocated blocks shrink
  maturity measured
  owns EstateDensityLedger
  source_path scripts/reclaim_space.mjs
  source_path scripts/release/public_surface_rollout.mjs
  source_path .claude/skills/density/SKILL.md
  source_path /Users/nickgonzales/.bonfyre/density/tools/clone_apply.sh
  source_path /Users/nickgonzales/.bonfyre/density/tools/afsc_apply.sh
  source_path /Users/nickgonzales/.bonfyre/density/tools/census.sh
  source_path /Users/nickgonzales/.bonfyre/density/tools/unshared.mjs
  source_path /Users/nickgonzales/.bonfyre/density/releases-excluded-live-rollback-referenced-20261030.txt
  internal_calculus clone: group regular files by size then sha256; for each rewritten file clonefile the group's source to a sibling temp, restore mode and times, cmp byte-compare against the original, then rename over it; files outside the destination set (live, rollback or referenced releases) serve only as read-only clone sources
  internal_calculus transparent: ditto --hfsCompression to a sibling temp, keep only when allocated blocks shrink, cmp byte-compare, restore mode and times, re-check the original mtime, rename; skip open, hard-linked, already compressed, clone-shared (EF_SHARES_ALL_BLOCKS), under 8 KiB, or modified within six hours
  internal_calculus physical measurement is df on /System/Volumes/Data; du is clone-blind and only reflects transparent compression
  witness 2026-10-30 ~/.bonfyre/density ledgers: clone-releases 6,512 files (4.95 GB logical) in 113 unreferenced release trees, clone-estate-local 412 files, clone-operator 297 files; every ledger row re-hashed afterwards to its recorded sha256 with zero mismatches
  witness 2026-10-30 ~/.bonfyre/density ledgers: transparent compression caches 1,573 files 1,896,184 to 775,696 KiB, operator 500 files 946,044 to 252,312 KiB, estate-local 1,987 files 1,816,684 to 461,440 KiB; every row re-hashed to its recorded sha256 with zero mismatches
  witness 2026-10-30 df available 2,384,248 KiB before, 6,014,144 KiB after; release clone step alone measured +314,184 KiB because most release copies already shared blocks from an earlier reclaim dedupe
  invariant no original is replaced before a byte compare of its replacement passes; the rename is atomic and keeps path, bytes, mode and mtime
  invariant live, rollback and otherwise referenced release trees (LaunchAgent plists, open files, ~/.bonfyre references, one previous-service level) are never rewritten
  invariant canonical SQLite stores, WAL/SHM, keys, locks, open files, model weights and operator.sqlite3 and its backups are never rewritten
  forbidden_inference du shrinking -> physical bytes freed; clones are counted in full by du, and only df measures shared blocks
  forbidden_inference a file flagged compressed or cloned -> a different file; readers get identical bytes, and the ledger digest is of the original content
  forbidden_inference available bytes rising -> the 10 GiB reserve or a ResourceAdmission pass is met; the reserve is judged by the admission owner, not by this layer
  forbidden_inference clone or transparent density at the filesystem -> the writer was fixed; release staging still copies per release and keeps producing duplicates until its owner clones
  known_gap release staging now clones site/ and browser/ with COPYFILE_FICLONE (2026-10-30, scripts/release/public_surface_rollout.mjs; a 200 MB cpSync clone test moved df by 0 KiB with identical bytes), but frozen bin/ inputs are still written fresh per release; 77 live, rollback or referenced releases hold up to about 778 MiB of unshared duplicates that need the owner's approval
  known_gap model weights (19.7 GB) have no byte-identical duplicates and are resident, so no lossless reduction was taken; decmpfs would also slow mmap loads
  known_gap available space reached 5.7 GiB, short of the 10 GiB reserve
  known_gap Chrome's and VS Code ShipIt's caches belong to running apps and were not touched
  source_lineage operator goal a4ed1ecfa75b49f9a6e1f4710116589f; memory estate-physical-density-layer (density lives at the filesystem layer, never re-encoding)
  interacts estate-density-defers-cold-releases-to-retirement-archive

